<title>JAPAN: SHINAGAWA REFRACTORIES TO BUILD SHOPPING CENTRE.</title>
<headline>SHINAGAWA REFRACTORIES TO BUILD SHOPPING CENTRE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shinagawa Refractories Co Ltd said on Thursday it would invest about 11.5 billion yen to build a shopping centre in Nagoya, central Japan.  </p>
<p>The outlet, to have a floor space of 120,790 square metres, will be built on unused land that Shinagawa owns, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The shopping centre will be rented to supermarket chain operator Jusco Co Ltd and is scheduled to open in April 1999, the statement said.</p>
</text>
